 "storyArc": "Saturday is chaos. On Friday Tomás went to Paloquemao market and bought forty kilos of the wrong flour; the espresso machine died at 7:05; Vale made coffee in a pot like Rosa used to. Then Hernando's taxi-driver friends arrived, then their wives, and by Sunday night they had sold three hundred tintos. Tomás writes the total on the wall: $412.000. Twenty-eight days to go."
